#
# ********************************************************************
#
# Details about the fields are available in 
#   the LinuxCNC 2.9.4 System Manual
#   §12 Virtual Control Panels, starting on 
#   pg. 952
#
# ********************************************************************

# ********************************************************************
# Configuration values
#
#                                 Home   PCB
#  Axis  Joint  Channel   Type     Seq  Plug  Comments
#  ----  -----  -------  -------  ----  ----  ------------------------
#   X      0       02    LINEAR     1    P13
#   Y      -       --    ------     -         Not available as LATHE=1
#   Z      1       00    LINEAR     2    P11
#
#   A      -       08    ANGULAR    -    --   Not currently assigned to
#                                              a channel. Has its own
#                                              panel ENA-toggle chain
#                                              since 18 September 2026
#                                              (see below).
#   B      2       06    ANGULAR    3    P17   Panel ENA-toggle chain
#                                              restored 19 September
#                                              2026 (Rosetta_Panel_v1.ui
#                                              gave B its own row back,
#                                              independent of A's - see
#                                              CLAUDE.md).
#   C      -       09    ANGULAR    -    --   Not currently assigned to
#                                              a channel. Got its own
#                                              panel ENA-toggle chain 19
#                                              September 2026, same
#                                              pattern as A/B.
#
#   U      3       04    LINEAR     4    P15
#   V      4       01    LINEAR     5    P12
#   W      5       03    LINEAR     6    P14
#
#  Sp0     7       05      n/a     n/a   P16
#  Sp1     6       07      n/a     n/a   P18  Previously the C axis
# ********************************************************************

# ********************************************************************
# Setup the variables needed for the PyVCP Virtual Control Panels

# ENA buttons (Sp0, Sp1, X, Z, U, V, W, A, B, C) are momentary HAL_Buttons;
# each click toggles that axis's enable via a flipflop (a D-type
# flip-flop - pins: data, clk, set, reset, out - made into a toggle
# by feeding its own inverted output back into "data", so each clk
# rising edge flips "out" without the button staying visually
# pressed in). Every axis also ANDs in an independent "allow" pin
# (<Axis>_Ena_Override), so the external Rosetta_Settings configurator
# program can force any axis disabled regardless of its panel
# button's state, e.g. while changing that axis's scale.
#
# The pin lives on the main panel's own always-running HAL component
# ("gladevcp"), not on Rosetta_Settings - until 4 September 2026 it was
# owned by the embedded Settings tab's component (REBCnfg), but that
# component no longer exists once the Settings tab was replaced by the
# standalone Rosetta_Settings program. Hosting it on the main panel instead
# means its existence (and default TRUE value) doesn't depend on
# whether Rosetta_Settings happens to be running - Rosetta_Settings writes to
# it purely via `halcmd sets <letter>-ena-settings-allow ...` (the
# signal, not the pin - a netted pin can't be setp'd directly), the
# same as the main panel's own _clear_ena_override() already does in
# the other direction.
#
# X/Z/U/V/W/A/B/C also AND in "machine-is-on" (a second and2 stage,
# <axis>-estop-and) before the result reaches <axis>-enable - without
# it, hm2_7i92.0.stepgen.NN.enable for these joints was driven solely by
# the panel-toggle/override chain above, with no path back to E-stop/
# machine-off at all (confirmed live: pressing E-stop did not stop
# these axes). Sp0/Sp1 don't need this same second stage: their
# stepgen.06/07.enable pins are already wired directly to
# "machine-is-on" in Rosetta.hal, bypassing their own panel-toggle chain
# entirely for the actual hardware enable - this brings these axes up
# to that same guarantee, just via an extra AND stage since their
# stepgen.enable pins are driven by <axis>-enable (the panel-toggle
# net) rather than by machine-is-on directly.
#
# B and C got the same chain 19 September 2026, once Rosetta_Panel_v1.ui
# gave every one of the 8 axis letters its own permanent, independent
# row (no more one letter's ENA button standing in for another's
# channel slot - see CLAUDE.md). Every axis letter now has this chain;
# only Sp0/Sp1 stay on their simpler stepgen.enable-direct-to-
# machine-is-on pattern (see above).
#
# All instances of a given realtime component must be declared in a
# single loadrt line - the underlying kernel module can only be
# inserted once.
loadrt flipflop names=sp0-ena-flip,sp1-ena-flip,x-ena-flip,z-ena-flip,u-ena-flip,v-ena-flip,w-ena-flip,a-ena-flip,b-ena-flip,c-ena-flip
loadrt not names=sp0-ena-not,sp1-ena-not,x-ena-not,z-ena-not,u-ena-not,v-ena-not,w-ena-not,a-ena-not,b-ena-not,c-ena-not
loadrt and2 names=x-ena-and,z-ena-and,u-ena-and,v-ena-and,w-ena-and,sp0-ena-and,sp1-ena-and,x-estop-and,z-estop-and,u-estop-and,v-estop-and,w-estop-and,a-ena-and,a-estop-and,b-ena-and,b-estop-and,c-ena-and,c-estop-and

# ******************************************
# Spindles

addf sp0-ena-not servo-thread
addf sp1-ena-not servo-thread
addf sp0-ena-flip servo-thread
addf sp1-ena-flip servo-thread
addf sp0-ena-and servo-thread
addf sp1-ena-and servo-thread

# net spindle.0-vel-cmd-rpm                  => gladevcp.Sp0_Spd
net sp0-ena-btn                          <= gladevcp.Sp0_ENA-button
net sp0-ena-btn                          => sp0-ena-flip.clk
net sp0-ena-panel                        <= sp0-ena-flip.out
net sp0-ena-panel                        => sp0-ena-and.in0
net sp0-ena-panel                        => sp0-ena-not.in
net sp0-ena-panel-inv                    <= sp0-ena-not.out
net sp0-ena-panel-inv                    => sp0-ena-flip.data
net sp0-ena-settings-allow               <= gladevcp.Sp0_Ena_Override
net sp0-ena-settings-allow               => sp0-ena-and.in1
net spindle.0-enable                     <= sp0-ena-and.out
net spindle.0-enable                     => gladevcp.Sp0_ENA-light

# net spindle.1-vel-cmd-rpm                  => gladevcp.Sp1_Spd
net sp1-ena-btn                          <= gladevcp.Sp1_ENA-button
net sp1-ena-btn                          => sp1-ena-flip.clk
net sp1-ena-panel                        <= sp1-ena-flip.out
net sp1-ena-panel                        => sp1-ena-and.in0
net sp1-ena-panel                        => sp1-ena-not.in
net sp1-ena-panel-inv                    <= sp1-ena-not.out
net sp1-ena-panel-inv                    => sp1-ena-flip.data
net sp1-ena-settings-allow               <= gladevcp.Sp1_Ena_Override
net sp1-ena-settings-allow               => sp1-ena-and.in1
net spindle.1-enable                     <= sp1-ena-and.out
net spindle.1-enable                     => gladevcp.Sp1_ENA-light

# ******************************************
# Rotary Axes

addf a-ena-not servo-thread
addf a-ena-flip servo-thread
addf a-ena-and servo-thread
addf a-estop-and servo-thread

net a-ena-btn                            <= gladevcp.A_ENA-button
net a-ena-btn                            => a-ena-flip.clk
net a-ena-panel                          <= a-ena-flip.out
net a-ena-panel                          => a-ena-and.in0
net a-ena-panel                          => a-ena-not.in
net a-ena-panel-inv                      <= a-ena-not.out
net a-ena-panel-inv                      => a-ena-flip.data
net a-ena-settings-allow                 <= gladevcp.A_Ena_Override
net a-ena-settings-allow                 => a-ena-and.in1
net a-ena-panel-allow                    <= a-ena-and.out
net a-ena-panel-allow                    => a-estop-and.in0
net machine-is-on                        => a-estop-and.in1
net a-enable                             <= a-estop-and.out
net a-enable                             => gladevcp.A_ENA-light

addf b-ena-not servo-thread
addf b-ena-flip servo-thread
addf b-ena-and servo-thread
addf b-estop-and servo-thread

# Restored 19 September 2026 - B had this same chain until 18 September,
# when its Rosetta_Panel_v1.ui widget (B_ENA) was temporarily replaced by
# A_ENA (A had no row of its own yet and needed a real enable control
# more urgently than B, which still had machine-is-on as a working
# fallback). Rosetta_Panel_v1.ui now gives every axis letter its own
# permanent row, so B gets its real chain back, independent of A's.
net b-ena-btn                            <= gladevcp.B_ENA-button
net b-ena-btn                            => b-ena-flip.clk
net b-ena-panel                          <= b-ena-flip.out
net b-ena-panel                          => b-ena-and.in0
net b-ena-panel                          => b-ena-not.in
net b-ena-panel-inv                      <= b-ena-not.out
net b-ena-panel-inv                      => b-ena-flip.data
net b-ena-settings-allow                 <= gladevcp.B_Ena_Override
net b-ena-settings-allow                 => b-ena-and.in1
net b-ena-panel-allow                    <= b-ena-and.out
net b-ena-panel-allow                    => b-estop-and.in0
net machine-is-on                        => b-estop-and.in1
net b-enable                             <= b-estop-and.out
net b-enable                             => gladevcp.B_ENA-light

addf c-ena-not servo-thread
addf c-ena-flip servo-thread
addf c-ena-and servo-thread
addf c-estop-and servo-thread

# Added 19 September 2026 - C previously had no panel ENA-toggle chain
# at all (no main-panel widget existed for it - "engine only" scope,
# 13 September 2026) and its Rosetta.hal enable consumer was wired straight
# to "machine-is-on", so C could never be disabled independently of the
# whole machine. Same pattern as A/B above.
net c-ena-btn                            <= gladevcp.C_ENA-button
net c-ena-btn                            => c-ena-flip.clk
net c-ena-panel                          <= c-ena-flip.out
net c-ena-panel                          => c-ena-and.in0
net c-ena-panel                          => c-ena-not.in
net c-ena-panel-inv                      <= c-ena-not.out
net c-ena-panel-inv                      => c-ena-flip.data
net c-ena-settings-allow                 <= gladevcp.C_Ena_Override
net c-ena-settings-allow                 => c-ena-and.in1
net c-ena-panel-allow                    <= c-ena-and.out
net c-ena-panel-allow                    => c-estop-and.in0
net machine-is-on                        => c-estop-and.in1
net c-enable                             <= c-estop-and.out
net c-enable                             => gladevcp.C_ENA-light

# ******************************************
# Linear Axes

# net x-vel-cmd                          => gladevcp.X_Spd
# net x-pos-fb                           => gladevcp.X_DRO

addf x-ena-not servo-thread
addf x-ena-flip servo-thread
addf x-ena-and servo-thread
addf x-estop-and servo-thread

net x-ena-btn                            <= gladevcp.X_ENA-button
net x-ena-btn                            => x-ena-flip.clk
net x-ena-panel                          <= x-ena-flip.out
net x-ena-panel                          => x-ena-and.in0
net x-ena-panel                          => x-ena-not.in
net x-ena-panel-inv                      <= x-ena-not.out
net x-ena-panel-inv                      => x-ena-flip.data
net x-ena-settings-allow                 <= gladevcp.X_Ena_Override
net x-ena-settings-allow                 => x-ena-and.in1
net x-ena-panel-allow                    <= x-ena-and.out
net x-ena-panel-allow                    => x-estop-and.in0
net machine-is-on                        => x-estop-and.in1
net x-enable                             <= x-estop-and.out
net x-enable                             => gladevcp.X_ENA-light

# net y-vel-cmd                          => gladevcp.Y_Spd
# net y-pos-fb                           => gladevcp.Y_DRO
# net y-enable                           => gladevcp.Y_ENA_Status
# net y-enable                          <=  gladevcp.Y_ENA

addf z-ena-not servo-thread
addf u-ena-not servo-thread
addf v-ena-not servo-thread
addf w-ena-not servo-thread
addf z-ena-flip servo-thread
addf u-ena-flip servo-thread
addf v-ena-flip servo-thread
addf w-ena-flip servo-thread
addf z-ena-and servo-thread
addf u-ena-and servo-thread
addf v-ena-and servo-thread
addf w-ena-and servo-thread
addf z-estop-and servo-thread
addf u-estop-and servo-thread
addf v-estop-and servo-thread
addf w-estop-and servo-thread

# net z-vel-cmd                          => gladevcp.Z_Spd
# net z-pos-fb                           => gladevcp.Z_DRO
net z-ena-btn                            <= gladevcp.Z_ENA-button
net z-ena-btn                            => z-ena-flip.clk
net z-ena-panel                          <= z-ena-flip.out
net z-ena-panel                          => z-ena-and.in0
net z-ena-panel                          => z-ena-not.in
net z-ena-panel-inv                      <= z-ena-not.out
net z-ena-panel-inv                      => z-ena-flip.data
net z-ena-settings-allow                 <= gladevcp.Z_Ena_Override
net z-ena-settings-allow                 => z-ena-and.in1
net z-ena-panel-allow                    <= z-ena-and.out
net z-ena-panel-allow                    => z-estop-and.in0
net machine-is-on                        => z-estop-and.in1
net z-enable                             <= z-estop-and.out
net z-enable                             => gladevcp.Z_ENA-light

# net u-vel-cmd                          => gladevcp.U_Spd
# net u-pos-fb                           => gladevcp.U_DRO
net u-ena-btn                            <= gladevcp.U_ENA-button
net u-ena-btn                            => u-ena-flip.clk
net u-ena-panel                          <= u-ena-flip.out
net u-ena-panel                          => u-ena-and.in0
net u-ena-panel                          => u-ena-not.in
net u-ena-panel-inv                      <= u-ena-not.out
net u-ena-panel-inv                      => u-ena-flip.data
net u-ena-settings-allow                 <= gladevcp.U_Ena_Override
net u-ena-settings-allow                 => u-ena-and.in1
net u-ena-panel-allow                    <= u-ena-and.out
net u-ena-panel-allow                    => u-estop-and.in0
net machine-is-on                        => u-estop-and.in1
net u-enable                             <= u-estop-and.out
net u-enable                             => gladevcp.U_ENA-light

# net v-vel-cmd                          => gladevcp.V_Spd
# net v-pos-fb                           => gladevcp.V_DRO
net v-ena-btn                            <= gladevcp.V_ENA-button
net v-ena-btn                            => v-ena-flip.clk
net v-ena-panel                          <= v-ena-flip.out
net v-ena-panel                          => v-ena-and.in0
net v-ena-panel                          => v-ena-not.in
net v-ena-panel-inv                      <= v-ena-not.out
net v-ena-panel-inv                      => v-ena-flip.data
net v-ena-settings-allow                 <= gladevcp.V_Ena_Override
net v-ena-settings-allow                 => v-ena-and.in1
net v-ena-panel-allow                    <= v-ena-and.out
net v-ena-panel-allow                    => v-estop-and.in0
net machine-is-on                        => v-estop-and.in1
net v-enable                             <= v-estop-and.out
net v-enable                             => gladevcp.V_ENA-light

# net w-vel-cmd                          => gladevcp.W_Spd
# net w-pos-fb                           => gladevcp.W_DRO
net w-ena-btn                            <= gladevcp.W_ENA-button
net w-ena-btn                            => w-ena-flip.clk
net w-ena-panel                          <= w-ena-flip.out
net w-ena-panel                          => w-ena-and.in0
net w-ena-panel                          => w-ena-not.in
net w-ena-panel-inv                      <= w-ena-not.out
net w-ena-panel-inv                      => w-ena-flip.data
net w-ena-settings-allow                 <= gladevcp.W_Ena_Override
net w-ena-settings-allow                 => w-ena-and.in1
net w-ena-panel-allow                    <= w-ena-and.out
net w-ena-panel-allow                    => w-estop-and.in0
net machine-is-on                        => w-estop-and.in1
net w-enable                             <= w-estop-and.out
net w-enable                             => gladevcp.W_ENA-light

# ******************************************
# Sp0/Sp1 simultaneous indexing

# Sp0-idx-angle/Sp0-idx-active/Sp1-idx-angle/Sp1-idx-active are created
# (with readers only - mux2.2/mux2.3/or2.0/or2.1) in Rosetta.hal, since
# their driver, the GladeVCP main panel's own pins, doesn't exist until
# the panel process starts - same reason the ENA override pins above
# are wired here rather than in Rosetta.hal. See Rosetta_main.py's
# _index_both_spindles_simultaneously and Rosetta.hal's Sp0/Sp1 blocks.
net Sp0-idx-angle                        <= gladevcp.Sp0-idx-angle
net Sp0-idx-active                       <= gladevcp.Sp0-idx-active
net Sp1-idx-angle                        <= gladevcp.Sp1-idx-angle
net Sp1-idx-active                       <= gladevcp.Sp1-idx-active

# ******************************************
# Main panel enable/disable

# Grays out the whole main panel (Rosetta_Panel_v1.ui) until the machine
# is powered on. machine-is-on is defined in Rosetta.hal, driven by
# halui.machine.is-on.
net machine-is-on                        => gladevcp.machine-is-on

# ******************************************
# Threading tab progress

# Rosetta_Subroutines/rosetta_thread.ngc reports which pass it's on through
# motion.analog-out-00 (M67 E0) - Rosetta_main.py's _on_thread_status shows
# it on the Threading tab.
net thread-status                        motion.analog-out-00 => gladevcp.thread-status
